;;; -*- mode: auto-fill; mode: org; -*-
See =(info "(standards) NEWS File")=. User facing changes per release
are to be recorded here.

* Version 0.4.0
- Add =seshat-reader-dark-tint= (default =charcoal=) with five presets.
  Dark mode no longer inverts the page full range: pixel luminance is
  mapped onto two colours, so a dark background keeps a readable
  contrast instead of going pure black. =graphite= keeps the old
  full-range inversion + gamma and is the one-step way back.
- Dark mode is now a process-wide preference rather than a property of
  the open document: it survives reloading the file or opening another
  one, and turning it off keeps the chosen palette for next time.
- =seshat-reader-dyn--doc-invert= no longer needs an open document.
  New module function =seshat-reader-dyn--doc-tint= sets the two colours
  (=BG= / =FG= as =#xRRGGBB=), and =-1 -1= clears the tint again.
- New command =seshat-reader-dark-tint-cycle= steps through the five
  presets in table order (=graphite=, =midnight=, =charcoal=,
  =night-sepia=, =sepia=; the last one wraps around to the first) and
  repaints the open buffers as it goes. A negative prefix argument
  steps backwards. When the current value is a custom =(BG . FG)= cons
  or =nil=, cycling starts from the first preset. It turns dark mode on
  for you when dark mode is off, and in a non-reader buffer it only
  changes the global preference. The package binds no key to it; bind
  it in your own config if you want one.
- Changing =seshat-reader-dark-tint= does not repaint open buffers:
  step through the presets with =seshat-reader-dark-tint-cycle= to
  repaint as you go, or toggle =seshat-reader-dark-mode= again or press
  =C-l=.
- Note: the tint maps every pixel onto a two-colour ramp, so colour
  figures and covers become monochrome; the =sepia= preset also makes
  the existing yellow highlight decorations hard to see.
- Per window pages, zooming, etc. support, which means that it is now
  possible to view different pages of the same document (from the same
  buffer) on different windows.
- Change 'screenful' to 'screen' in command names.
- Make =reader-reset-size= interactive.
- Overall stability improvements when opening files, accessing
  bookmarks, and outlines.
- Remove F5 keybinding for =reader-presentation-mode=.
- Remove =reader-mode= as an interactive command.
- Fix weird page border artifacts when using the mouse.
- Add =reader-build= command to automatically build the dynamic module.

* Version 0.3.2
- Fix reader-outline when original source buffer is killed.
- Correct keybindings for C-v/M-v.
- Enhance build system on GNU/Linux and MS Windows.

* Version 0.3.1
- Start NEWS file.
- Fix MS Windows build.
- Fix the order of reader outline, where the last heading would show
  up at the beginning, now they show up at the end.
- Fix bug where setting the left-fringe-width would disable the
  centering.
- Add new customize option, =reader-default-fit=, for setting the
  default fitting (fit to height or fit to width).
- Add a new command, =reader-reset-size=, to reset scaling to 1.0.
- Fix scrolling when =pixel-scroll-precision-mode= is enabled.
- Fix =revert-buffer= to respect the theme, page and scale of the document.
